<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mensheviks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mensheviks were the moderate faction of the Russian Social Democratic Labour Party, formed when it split with Lenin's Bolsheviks in 1903. Led by Julius Martov and others, they favoured a broad party and a bourgeois-democratic stage before socialism. They took part in the Provisional Government of 1917, governed independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1918 to 1921 and were suppressed by the Soviet regime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mensheviks.jpg" alt="Mensheviks" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mensevikii.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
